%N A397782 Number of nonisomorphic rectangular doppelsemigroups of order n.
%C A397782 A doppelsemigroup is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A397782    (x -| y) |- z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A397782    (x |- y) -| z = x |- (y -| z).
%C A397782 A doppelsemigroup (D,-|,|-) is called rectangular if both (D,-|) and (D,|-) are rectangular semigroups in the sense that
%C A397782    x -| y -| z = x -| z and x |- y |- z = x |- z
%C A397782 for all x,y,z from D.
%H A397782 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="/A397782/b397782.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..100</a>
%H A397782 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2606.28908">Note on the number of doppelsemigroups of small order</a>, arXiv:2606.28908 [math.GR] (2026).
%H A397782 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.15421/242602">Note on the number of doppelsemigroups of small order</a>, Res. Math. 34(1) (2026), 16-33.
%H A397782 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23242506">Enumeration and lists of nonisomorphic rectangular doppelsemigroups</a>, Zenodo (2026).
%H A397782 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/74db88819780c1ce108e080ecc1cd964">C++ program for computing all pairwise nonisomorphic rectangular doppelsemigroups</a>, GitHub Gist (2026).
%e A397782 For n = 3, there are exactly 7 pairwise nonisomorphic rectangular doppelsemigroups (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1,2}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1,2. The Cayley tables of all seven doppelsemigroups are listed below.
%e A397782 Doppelsemigroup #1:
%e A397782    -|:     |-:
%e A397782    0 0 0   0 0 0
%e A397782    0 0 0   0 0 0
%e A397782    0 0 0   0 0 0
%e A397782 Doppelsemigroup #2:
%e A397782    -|:     |-:
%e A397782    0 0 0   0 0 0
%e A397782    1 1 1   1 1 1
%e A397782    2 2 2   2 2 2
%e A397782 Doppelsemigroup #3:
%e A397782    -|:     |-:
%e A397782    0 1 2   0 1 2
%e A397782    0 1 2   0 1 2
%e A397782    0 1 2   0 1 2
%e A397782 Doppelsemigroup #4:
%e A397782    -|:     |-:
%e A397782    0 0 0   0 0 0
%e A397782    1 1 1   1 1 1
%e A397782    0 0 0   0 0 0
%e A397782 Doppelsemigroup #5:
%e A397782    -|:     |-:
%e A397782    0 1 0   0 1 0
%e A397782    0 1 0   0 1 0
%e A397782    0 1 0   0 1 0
%e A397782 Doppelsemigroup #6:
%e A397782    -|:     |-:
%e A397782    0 0 0   0 0 0
%e A397782    1 1 1   1 1 1
%e A397782    0 0 0   1 1 1
%e A397782 Doppelsemigroup #7:
%e A397782    -|:     |-:
%e A397782    0 1 0   0 1 1
%e A397782    0 1 0   0 1 1
%e A397782    0 1 0   0 1 1
